{
  "id": 493267491,
  "iid": 25288,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "Qt: Don't install the binary translations a second time on Windows",
  "description": "The wireshark_ QM files are embedded into the executables via the\nresource system. It doesn't make sense to ship them separately in\nthe translations/ directory. While someone could substitute their\nown translation and place it in the languages subdirectory of the\nglobal datadir or personal configuration directory, it's not really\nplausible to edit the binary QM files to do so. Instead, someone\nwould need to get the source TS files from the repository (or generate\nthem for a new language with Qt Linguist Tools), make any edits, and\ncompile them into QM files.\n\nThis frees up somewhat over 6 MB of installed space on Windows.\n\nAlso add some comments about MinGW systems, where the Qt system\ntranslation catalogs are not properly deployed by windeployqt.\n\nAI-Assisted: no",
  "state": "merged",
  "created_at": "2026-06-07T12:41:47.840Z",
